pgp and pkcs#7
--------------


PGP (Pretty Good Privacy)
🔹 Purpose: Used for file encryption and secure data exchange
🔹 Encryption Method: Asymmetric encryption with public-private key pairs
🔹 Key Management: Requires PGP key pairs (Public & Private Keys)
🔹 Supported Algorithms: RSA, AES, CAST5, TripleDES
🔹 Usage in SAP CPI: Implemented via PGP Encryptor & PGP Decryptor
🔹 Best for: Securing file transfers and protecting sensitive data


PKCS#7 (Public Key Cryptography Standards #7)
🔹 Purpose: Used for secure message exchange in web services and APIs
🔹 Encryption Method: Based on CMS (Cryptographic Message Syntax)
🔹 Key Management: Uses X.509 certificates for encryption
🔹 Supported Algorithms: AES, DES, RC2, Camellia, etc.
🔹 Usage in SAP CPI: Implemented via PKCS#7 Encryptor & PKCS#7 Decryptor
🔹 Best for: B2B integrations and encrypted API communications

Which One to Use?
✔ PGP → Best for securing file transfers & emails
✔ PKCS#7 → Ideal for message encryption in web services & APIs



